    "slug": "somali-parliament-concludes-debate-on-central-bank-amendment-bill",
    "summary": "The House of the People wrapped up its second reading of a bill to amend the Central Bank of Somalia law, with 141 MPs present. The debate is part of ongoing efforts to strengthen the financial sector.",
    "content": "Mogadishu, Somalia – The House of the People of the Federal Parliament of Somalia held its 22nd session of the 8th term on Saturday, chaired by Speaker Abdulqadir Mohamed Nur (Jaamac). The session, which opened with a quorum of 141 MPs, focused on the second reading of a bill to amend the Central Bank of Somalia Law (Law LR.130, issued on 22 April 2024).\n\nThe debate is part of a broader legislative effort to update the legal framework governing the Central Bank. The proposed amendments aim to enhance the bank's autonomy and align its operations with international best practices, according to parliamentary sources. This follows earlier discussions in the House on the importance of a robust financial system for Somalia's economic recovery.\n\nThe Central Bank of Somalia has been undergoing reforms in recent years, including the introduction of a new currency and efforts to strengthen anti-money laundering measures. The amendment bill is seen as a key step in these reforms, which are supported by international partners such as the International Monetary Fund and the World Bank.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, which remits billions of dollars annually and plays a vital role in the country's economy, a stronger and more transparent Central Bank is crucial. It can help ensure the stability of the Somali shilling, facilitate formal remittance channels, and create a more conducive environment for investment. Diaspora members have long called for improved financial governance to protect their remittances and foster economic development.\n\nThe House is expected to proceed to a third reading and final vote on the bill in the coming sessions. If passed, the amendments will mark a significant milestone in Somalia's efforts to build a modern and resilient financial sector.",
